{"title":"Kawahara capillary–gravity waves","markdown":{"headingText":"Kawahara capillary–gravity waves","headingAttr":{"id":"sec-kawahara","classes":[],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n`apps/kawahara` — the only *dispersive* model in the report: fifth order, and\nits linear symbol is purely imaginary.\n\n## Physical setting\n\nLong weakly nonlinear waves on a shallow fluid layer where surface tension and\ngravity both matter. Where the Korteweg–de Vries equation keeps only\nthird-order dispersion, Kawahara (1972) retains the fifth-order term as well.\nWhen the two have opposite signs they compete, and the resulting dispersion\nrelation is non-monotonic — waves of different length can travel in opposite\ndirections.\n\n## Governing equations\n\n$$\n\\partial_t u \\;+\\; \\alpha\\,u\\,\\partial_x u\n  \\;-\\; \\beta\\,\\partial_x^3 u\n  \\;+\\; \\gamma\\,\\partial_x^5 u \\;=\\; 0 .\n$$ {#eq-kw-pde}\n\n::: {.callout-note}\n## Sign convention\n\nThis application defines $\\beta$ with a minus sign in @eq-kw-pde. To use a\ncoefficient $b$ multiplying $+u_{xxx}$, set $\\beta = -b$.\n:::\n\n## Spectral formulation\n\nOdd derivatives transform to odd powers of $ik$, so the symbol is **purely\nimaginary**:\n\n$$\nL(k) \\;=\\; -i\\,\\omega(k), \\qquad \\omega(k) \\;=\\; \\beta k^3 + \\gamma k^5 .\n$$ {#eq-kw-symbol}\n\nThe quadratic flux $\\alpha u\\,\\partial_x u = \\tfrac{\\alpha}{2}\\partial_x(u^2)$\nis evaluated as $N = u^2$ with\n\n$$\nM_{\\mathrm{nl}}(k) \\;=\\; -i\\,\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\,k_x .\n$$ {#eq-kw-nl}\n\nThis is the qualitative difference from every other spectral chapter here.\nAn even-order dissipative operator has $L$ real and negative: $|e^{L\\Delta t}|<1$\nand modes **decay**. Here $L$ is imaginary, so $|e^{L\\Delta t}| = 1$ exactly and\nmodes **rotate** — the amplitude of each Fourier component is preserved and only\nits phase advances. ETD is not damping anything; it is applying an exact phase\nrotation.\n\nThe phase velocity follows from @eq-kw-symbol:\n\n$$\nc_p(k) \\;=\\; \\frac{\\omega(k)}{k} \\;=\\; \\beta k^2 + \\gamma k^4 ,\n$$ {#eq-kw-phase}\n\nwhich changes sign at $k^2 = -\\beta/\\gamma$ when $\\beta\\gamma < 0$. Below that\nwave number waves travel one way, above it the other. The defaults\n$\\alpha = 1$, $\\beta = 1$, $\\gamma = -1$ put the model in this competing\nregime.\n\n## Solution strategy\n\nETD1 as in @eq-etd1, dealiased — the quadratic nonlinearity doubles the\nhighest wave number present, so the 2/3 rule is required.\n\n## Verification\n\n* **Phase velocity.** A single mode advances at $c_p(k)$ from\n  @eq-kw-phase, checked independently for the $k^3$ and $k^5$ branches.\n* **Manufactured solutions.** Independent manufactured-solution tests for\n  third- and fifth-order dispersion.\n* **Mean preservation.** The $\\mathbf{k}=0$ mode is untouched.\n\n## Binaries and inputs\n\n`kawahara` (CPU), `kawahara_hip`. Preset `pulse.json` (256-point line).\n\n## Scalability\n\nNot measured.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-run